01:07:23.550 --> 01:07:23.870
Silence!

01:07:26.450 --> 01:07:29.970
Why not El Supremo, the direct descendant of Jose Quin...

01:07:30.000 --> 01:07:39.000
And was not Jose Quintero the Almighty's right hand when Cortez carried his word to the Mexican heathens in interrupting me?

01:07:39.000 --> 01:07:43.300
You are interrupting God, who speaks through me.

01:07:47.590 --> 01:07:48.130
Do the punishment.

01:07:49.490 --> 01:07:54.860
And God says that for your failure, you must pay with your life.

01:08:00.000 --> 01:08:00.300
Thank you.

01:08:32.130 --> 01:08:34.470
That, then, is the leader of the man who attacked you.

01:08:35.090 --> 01:08:36.650
We call him El Diablo.

01:08:36.990 --> 01:08:39.850
He is El Supremo, the all-powerful, as we'll all soon find out.

01:08:39.930 --> 01:08:40.570
A mere nerd.

01:08:41.070 --> 01:08:42.590
Through him speaks the Inquisitor.

01:08:42.890 --> 01:08:43.910
Through him speaks God.

01:08:44.170 --> 01:08:45.770
Rubbish. God needs no interpreter.

01:08:46.110 --> 01:08:46.710
Later, chief.

01:08:48.640 --> 01:08:48.780
You?

01:08:49.550 --> 01:08:54.570
I'm Sarah. I was born on the island, as were my parents and their parents before them.

01:08:55.290 --> 01:08:59.630
We descended from settlers who were sailing to find release from social and religious persecution.

01:09:00.860 --> 01:09:02.260
And we still haven't found it.

01:09:02.560 --> 01:09:03.900
Nor will you, because you are weak.

01:09:05.420 --> 01:09:08.020
We work hard to survive, to grow food.

01:09:08.490 --> 01:09:09.950
While you do nothing.

01:09:10.460 --> 01:09:13.920
You're wicked people, stronger than we.

01:09:14.180 --> 01:09:15.660
El Supremo is stronger than all.

01:09:15.930 --> 01:09:18.050
All of you will soon know the island of El Supremo.

01:09:18.150 --> 01:09:19.750
Don't you be too sure, my lad.

01:09:20.330 --> 01:09:22.230
Right is a funny way of coming out on top.

01:09:22.290 --> 01:09:23.510
You talk like the slaves.

01:09:23.590 --> 01:09:24.730
The meek shall inherit the air.

01:09:25.440 --> 01:09:26.120
Perhaps they will.

01:09:27.020 --> 01:09:28.080
If they're strong, give it to them.

01:09:28.180 --> 01:09:29.720
I've met your account before, not content.

01:09:30.800 --> 01:09:38.530
all right now is not the time right stand to our watches on deck i'll take the first

01:09:38.530 --> 01:09:40.760
and the rest of you grab what sleep you can

01:10:01.820 --> 01:10:02.520
Here's some coffee.

01:10:02.680 --> 01:10:08.150
Where do you think we are?

01:10:09.980 --> 01:10:10.460
Somewhere there.

01:10:13.170 --> 01:10:13.910
There's nothing there.

01:10:19.130 --> 01:10:20.230
Think we ever get to Caracas?

01:10:21.950 --> 01:10:23.730
People thought that worried you one way or the other.

01:10:25.450 --> 01:10:28.060
Dad, our man is waiting for me.

01:10:29.060 --> 01:10:29.420
Figures.

01:10:30.890 --> 01:10:32.310
What is he, a Venezuelan oil magnet?

01:10:32.490 --> 01:10:38.070
I could imagine by now he's a very frightened little boy.

01:10:39.150 --> 01:10:41.750
My son, Captain, is eight years old.

01:10:44.080 --> 01:10:44.960
What's he doing in Caracas?

01:10:47.720 --> 01:10:48.440
Waiting for me.

01:10:49.490 --> 01:10:51.230
Come, you were in Africa and he was in South America.

01:10:52.400 --> 01:10:55.180
I didn't think you were interested in other people's problems.

01:10:58.320 --> 01:10:58.720
One night.

01:11:01.120 --> 01:11:01.760
It's a long story.

01:11:08.000 --> 01:11:12.060
Eleven years ago, I fell in love with a man.

01:11:13.300 --> 01:11:14.440
A great man, I thought.

01:11:14.960 --> 01:11:16.920
He was going to pull his country out of poverty.

01:11:17.040 --> 01:11:19.900
He said he loved me.

01:11:20.020 --> 01:11:22.650
He was married, of course.

01:11:22.650 --> 01:11:23.630
I became his mistress.

01:11:24.600 --> 01:11:25.060
We had a son.

01:11:26.400 --> 01:11:29.840
Six months ago, his country found out that he wasn't the idol.

01:11:30.000 --> 01:11:30.700
I thought he was.

01:11:31.960 --> 01:11:34.170
He was forced to escape in the middle of the night.

01:11:44.980 --> 01:11:49.580
Antonio Fuentes, president of Santa Dominica.

01:11:50.940 --> 01:11:52.060
The people's savior.

01:11:54.550 --> 01:11:56.490
And he left, he took 20 million dollars.

01:11:57.090 --> 01:11:57.590
Their money.

01:11:59.400 --> 01:11:59.980
You preferred the money?

01:12:00.030 --> 01:12:00.670
money, dear son.

01:12:31.080 --> 01:12:32.260
All right, I'm sorry.

01:12:34.180 --> 01:12:34.820
I said, I'm sorry.

01:12:40.290 --> 01:12:40.910
So you escaped.

01:12:43.250 --> 01:12:53.240
I was shooting.

01:12:53.420 --> 01:12:53.880
I was alone.

01:12:54.000 --> 01:12:54.860
My son was with friends.

01:12:56.660 --> 01:12:59.200
When you came to collect me, he said an escape route was ready.

01:13:00.190 --> 01:13:01.350
Our son was waiting.

01:13:01.590 --> 01:13:02.440
It was a lie.

01:13:05.320 --> 01:13:06.880
The airport, they forced me on the plane.

01:13:07.740 --> 01:13:09.440
I wanted to stay to go back to my son.

01:13:10.260 --> 01:13:12.860
He swore that he had arranged for him to join us.

01:13:13.310 --> 01:13:13.890
Another lie.

01:13:15.060 --> 01:13:17.540
He had six months.

01:13:18.180 --> 01:13:20.740
I waited, pleaded, and thought.

01:13:24.900 --> 01:13:25.500
He did nothing.

01:13:26.220 --> 01:13:26.840
Got what he wanted.

01:13:28.370 --> 01:13:28.950
Messed that.

01:13:31.120 --> 01:13:38.810
Yes, I stabbed him, didn't die, but in 24 hours of his going to hospital, the police arrived with my deportation papers.

01:13:39.800 --> 01:13:42.720
Still had some of her friends.

01:13:45.100 --> 01:13:48.780
One thing he forgot, I knew, or he kept the money.

01:13:53.770 --> 01:13:53.970
Bobby?

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:02.130
I needed to buy that, my son.

01:14:05.990 --> 01:14:08.280
Do you?

01:14:11.210 --> 01:14:14.440
Yes, I am sorry.

01:14:16.960 --> 01:14:17.880
Are you sorry?

01:14:18.410 --> 01:14:18.850
No.

01:14:19.050 --> 01:14:19.410
You're not?

01:14:19.690 --> 01:14:20.050
I'm sorry.

01:14:20.290 --> 01:14:20.930
I thought you said you weren't.

01:14:30.600 --> 01:14:34.510
Don't think that's very funny.

01:14:43.120 --> 01:14:44.380
Worried about your people?

01:14:47.090 --> 01:14:48.270
It's been three days now.

01:14:49.970 --> 01:14:53.170
They must think I'm dead or captured by the Spaniard.

01:15:03.520 --> 01:15:04.600
What, will he leave again?

01:15:05.350 --> 01:15:06.170
That's all we've got.

01:15:06.270 --> 01:15:07.070
Make the most of it.

01:15:07.340 --> 01:15:09.400
We've been thankful we're Christian-minded people, young man.

01:15:09.460 --> 01:15:10.360
You're eating our rafting.

01:15:10.480 --> 01:15:10.940
I know it.

01:15:11.360 --> 01:15:12.340
And I think you're fools.

01:15:13.010 --> 01:15:14.410
Why don't you just throw me off the side?

01:15:14.490 --> 01:15:15.750
Don't think we haven't thought about it.

01:15:15.770 --> 01:15:16.530
But you don't do it.

01:15:16.760 --> 01:15:17.360
That's the problem.

01:15:17.500 --> 01:15:19.460
I don't think it's what that limb of faith would do.

01:15:19.460 --> 01:15:20.380
He's not infallible.

01:15:20.860 --> 01:15:21.420
Where's Sarah?

01:15:21.840 --> 01:15:24.320
She was on deck just now, messing about with those balloon things.

01:15:40.460 --> 01:15:42.360
She's gone. I'm going after her.

01:15:49.380 --> 01:15:49.700
Lovely.

01:15:49.840 --> 01:15:51.600
Now, come on, Pat. Stop fooling her around.

01:15:53.340 --> 01:15:53.880
Come on, Chief.

01:16:00.120 --> 01:16:01.300
You don't find her quickly, come back.

01:16:01.900 --> 01:16:02.440
Right, sir.

01:16:41.690 --> 01:16:50.390
wouldn't like her to drop on me even if she was real any idea where we are chief well i thought

01:16:50.390 --> 01:16:59.900
the light should have been over our right shoulder no no the left we're lost i think we should go

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:10.830
back. We're back. I heard you calling. Thank God. Can you find a way back to the ship? In this? No.

01:17:11.970 --> 01:17:13.840
There's an island over there. Come on.

01:18:07.960 --> 01:18:17.650
call up a canoe and then we can all paddle our way back to the corridor sir okay you've got it

01:18:17.650 --> 01:18:24.920
gee all right if you'd like to try and get a bit of sleep sir i'll stay on watch

01:18:26.380 --> 01:18:28.220
go and have a bit of a rest

01:18:30.000 --> 01:18:30.780
Be careful, Pat.

01:18:31.140 --> 01:18:31.280
Yes.

01:18:33.340 --> 01:18:53.350
After you've said quite the risk, we'll have to make the most of it.

01:21:00.000 --> 01:21:00.720
Thank you.

01:22:00.000 --> 01:22:03.280
Oh, Chief, I think we should stay here till daybreak

01:22:03.280 --> 01:22:05.890
and then try and find our way back to the ship.

01:22:06.090 --> 01:22:06.690
You don't?

01:22:06.950 --> 01:22:29.360
To the Santa Anita.

01:22:34.000 --> 01:22:36.460
If not to Santa Anita, at least to Sportsman's Park.

01:22:39.090 --> 01:22:40.570
Now the conclusion of The Lost Continent,

01:22:40.570 --> 01:22:43.250
but first let's recreate the opening credits of the old Honeymooners TV show.

01:22:43.330 --> 01:22:43.710
Go ahead.

01:23:06.750 --> 01:23:09.670
Well, it means you can say goodbye to your friends.

01:23:10.610 --> 01:23:11.170
And what else?

01:23:25.090 --> 01:23:26.430
What was the meaning of that rocket?

01:24:28.700 --> 01:24:29.980
Join us and tell your competitors.

01:24:30.000 --> 01:24:36.380
on the boat to do likewise in which case all of your supplies will be turned over to us or else

01:24:36.380 --> 01:24:42.550
we shall kill you then kill your companions and take the supplies he'll kill us all anyway that

01:24:42.550 --> 01:24:50.240
is in the hands of god but if you pray to me he may find it in his heart i'll not pray to any man

01:24:50.240 --> 01:24:55.900
let alone a child who's hardly old enough to wipe his own bottom you are heretics and blasphemous

01:24:55.900 --> 01:24:59.960
there is no redemption for any of you you're the one who's blab

01:25:00.160 --> 01:25:02.870
Feaming? Oh, I'll bet the blame is mostly his.

01:25:03.160 --> 01:25:04.460
I am merely the servant.

01:25:04.980 --> 01:25:07.820
Funny sort of servant, getting a child to do your dirty work for you.

01:25:08.180 --> 01:25:09.580
Corrupting his mind so that he...

01:25:09.580 --> 01:25:09.980
Silence!

01:25:11.380 --> 01:25:12.860
Perhaps the lad's got a mind of his own.

01:25:13.760 --> 01:25:14.620
How about it, son?

01:25:15.610 --> 01:25:16.310
Don't you ever...

01:25:16.310 --> 01:25:18.400
Throw them into the village! All of them!

01:25:19.400 --> 01:25:25.890
Oh, stay where you are, all of you.

01:25:26.360 --> 01:25:26.440
Quick.

01:25:30.000 --> 01:25:31.440
What kind of a circus is this, anyway?

01:25:31.740 --> 01:25:34.820
You are in the court of El Supimo, the chosen one.

01:25:34.880 --> 01:25:36.320
He means the lads sitting on the throne.

01:25:36.700 --> 01:25:39.440
That boy, he's the one who paid the pint, huh?

01:25:39.660 --> 01:25:46.800
We can go noisily or quietly.

01:25:47.280 --> 01:25:48.000
Joyce is up to you.

01:25:48.200 --> 01:25:52.140
Where are you going? A trap here like the rest of us. No escape.

01:25:53.250 --> 01:25:54.610
How do you know? Have you ever tried?

01:25:55.410 --> 01:25:56.170
Ancestors tried.

01:25:56.450 --> 01:25:58.290
I'm not talking about them, I'm talking about you.

01:25:58.790 --> 01:25:59.770
It's God's will.

01:26:00.320 --> 01:26:02.200
It's your will because you want it this way.

01:26:02.950 --> 01:26:04.850
You do it in the name of God for this child here

01:26:04.850 --> 01:26:06.750
because you haven't got the guts to do your own dirty work.

01:26:07.080 --> 01:26:08.600
You speak bravely of escaping.

01:26:08.840 --> 01:26:09.740
How are you going to do it?

01:26:10.320 --> 01:26:11.440
I don't know, but we'll try.

01:26:12.080 --> 01:26:12.760
We'll fail.

01:26:13.400 --> 01:26:14.400
Then we'll go on trying.

01:26:14.540 --> 01:26:15.920
And the day we stop trying, we stop living.

01:26:18.340 --> 01:26:18.580
We're going.

01:26:21.040 --> 01:26:22.080
Trying with us is welcome.

01:26:23.150 --> 01:26:26.760
Well, stay where you are, all of you.

01:26:30.030 --> 01:26:31.150
Why not accept the inevitable?

01:26:32.180 --> 01:26:34.100
You're no longer masters of your own destiny.

01:26:34.840 --> 01:26:35.440
Join us.

01:26:35.650 --> 01:26:37.580
I'd rather chance the weed and die.

01:26:38.890 --> 01:26:39.410
And die.

01:27:30.636 --> 01:27:31.016
Thank you.

01:32:27.740 --> 01:32:29.960
called a lost continent? Did we even see a continent?

01:32:30.030 --> 01:32:30.810
Lost or otherwise?

01:32:31.190 --> 01:32:31.350
No.

01:32:31.630 --> 01:32:32.130
Well, okay.

01:32:32.350 --> 01:32:32.890
Sorry about that.

01:32:34.100 --> 01:32:37.100
You'll see the Phantom Planet next Saturday afternoon at 1.30.

01:32:37.340 --> 01:32:37.880
Good night, buddy.

01:32:38.120 --> 01:32:38.800
Wait a minute.

01:32:38.960 --> 01:32:39.180
What?

01:32:39.280 --> 01:32:40.540
I still got a joke to get in.

01:32:40.580 --> 01:32:41.160
No, come on.

01:32:41.220 --> 01:32:41.480
We're late.

01:32:41.540 --> 01:32:42.560
We can't be out of time already.

01:32:42.700 --> 01:32:43.700
Listen, this happens every week.

01:32:43.720 --> 01:32:44.620
I don't care who.

01:32:45.060 --> 01:32:46.460
And that's why you have, wait a minute.
